---
import MainLayout from "../layouts/MainLayout.astro";
---

<MainLayout
    title="The Tributaries | The River Kept Flowing"
    description="The Tributaries organize the many streams feeding The River Kept Flowing: faith, family, work, insurance, finance, health, food, philosophy, creation, and service."
>

<main data-pagefind-body>


        <header class="tributaries-hero">

            <div class="tributaries-hero-content">

                <p class="eyebrow">
                    The many streams feeding one life
                </p>

                <h1>
                    No river is sustained by a single source.
                </h1>

                <p class="tributaries-hero-lead">
                    Faith, family, work, health, knowledge, food, money, creativity,
                    service, and experience all enter the same life. The Tributaries
                    are where those streams are gathered, studied, and directed.
                </p>

                <div class="tributaries-hero-actions">

                    <a href="#tributary-map" class="button tributaries-button-primary">
                        Explore the Tributaries
                    </a>

                    <a href="#how-they-connect" class="button tributaries-button-secondary">
                        See How They Connect
                    </a>

                </div>

            </div>

        </header>


        <section class="tributaries-opening">

            <div class="reading-shell">

                <p class="section-label">
                    The structure of the river
                </p>

                <h2>
                    My life does not divide neatly into separate subjects.
                </h2>

                <p class="tributaries-opening-lead">
                    Everything flows into everything else.
                </p>

                <p>
                    Faith changes how I understand work.
                </p>

                <p>
                    Work changes how I understand responsibility.
                </p>

                <p>
                    Responsibility changes how I understand fatherhood, money,
                    time, health, and service.
                </p>

                <p>
                    Food becomes part of family culture. Exercise becomes part of
                    stewardship. Insurance becomes part of protection. Technology
                    becomes part of creation. Philosophy becomes part of every
                    decision made beneath the surface.
                </p>

                <p>
                    The Tributaries exist to organize those different streams
                    without pretending they are disconnected.
                </p>

                <p>
                    This is the map of what The River Kept Flowing is becoming.
                </p>

            </div>

        </section>


        <section class="tributaries-map" id="tributary-map">

            <div class="section-shell">

                <div class="tributaries-section-heading">

                    <p class="section-label light-label">
                        The tributary map
                    </p>

                    <h2>
                        Eleven streams feeding the larger work.
                    </h2>

                    <p>
                        Each tributary will eventually contain its own writings,
                        videos, guides, projects, lessons, and resources.
                    </p>

                </div>


                <div class="tributaries-grid">


                    <article class="tributary-card tributary-card-featured">

                        <span class="tributary-number">
                            01
                        </span>

                        <p class="tributary-type">
                            The deepest stream
                        </p>

                        <h3>
                            Faith & Calling
                        </h3>

                        <p>
                            Scripture, obedience, surrender, identity, prayer,
                            conviction, trust, purpose, temptation, distraction,
                            spiritual growth, and learning how to recognize what
                            God is asking of a life.
                        </p>

                        <div class="tributary-tags">

                            <span>Faith</span>
                            <span>Calling</span>
                            <span>Scripture</span>
                            <span>Obedience</span>

                        </div>

                        <a href="/river-guides/" class="tributary-link light-tributary-link">
                            Explore faith writings
                            <span aria-hidden="true">→</span>
                        </a>

                    </article>


                    <article class="tributary-card">

                        <span class="tributary-number">
                            02
                        </span>

                        <p class="tributary-type">
                            The people entrusted to me
                        </p>

                        <h3>
                            Family & Fatherhood
                        </h3>

                        <p>
                            Marriage, fatherhood, pregnancy, raising sons, family
                            leadership, presence, protection, household peace,
                            generational patterns, relationships, and the daily work
                            of learning how to love people well.
                        </p>

                        <div class="tributary-tags">

                            <span>Marriage</span>
                            <span>Fatherhood</span>
                            <span>Family</span>
                            <span>Legacy</span>

                        </div>

                        <a href="/letters-from-the-river/" class="tributary-link">
                            Read family reflections
                            <span aria-hidden="true">→</span>
                        </a>

                    </article>


                    <article class="tributary-card">

                        <span class="tributary-number">
                            03
                        </span>

                        <p class="tributary-type">
                            Creating value
                        </p>

                        <h3>
                            Business & Sales
                        </h3>

                        <p>
                            Sales psychology, communication, leadership, cold
                            outreach, warm leads, scripts, objections, follow-up,
                            systems, entrepreneurship, customer experience, and
                            learning how to create value without losing integrity.
                        </p>

                        <div class="tributary-tags">

                            <span>Sales</span>
                            <span>Leadership</span>
                            <span>Systems</span>
                            <span>Business</span>

                        </div>

                        <a href="/river-guides/" class="tributary-link">
                            Explore sales guides
                            <span aria-hidden="true">→</span>
                        </a>

                    </article>


                    <article class="tributary-card">

                        <span class="tributary-number">
                            04
                        </span>

                        <p class="tributary-type">
                            Protecting what matters
                        </p>

                        <h3>
                            Insurance
                        </h3>

                        <p>
                            Property and casualty coverage, policy structure,
                            insurable interests, errors and omissions, underwriting,
                            client education, agency operations, risk transfer,
                            claims preparation, and responsible protection.
                        </p>

                        <div class="tributary-tags">

                            <span>Home</span>
                            <span>Auto</span>
                            <span>Life</span>
                            <span>Risk</span>

                        </div>

                        <a href="/river-guides/" class="tributary-link">
                            Explore insurance education
                            <span aria-hidden="true">→</span>
                        </a>

