        </section>


        <section class="tributaries-connection" id="how-they-connect">

            <div class="section-shell tributaries-connection-grid">

                <div class="tributaries-connection-heading">

                    <p class="section-label">
                        How the streams connect
                    </p>

                    <h2>
                        No tributary remains isolated for long.
                    </h2>

                </div>


                <div class="tributaries-connection-body">

                    <p class="tributaries-connection-lead">
                        A problem in one stream eventually changes the whole river.
                    </p>

                    <p>
                        Financial pressure can weaken a marriage.
                    </p>

                    <p>
                        Poor health can reduce patience, clarity, productivity,
                        and presence.
                    </p>

                    <p>
                        Unexamined beliefs can distort work, money, relationships,
                        identity, and the meaning assigned to success.
                    </p>

                    <p>
                        A career can provide for a family while simultaneously
                        taking so much attention that the family rarely receives
                        the person doing the providing.
                    </p>

                    <p>
                        Technology can create freedom or consume it. Ambition can
                        create opportunity or become another form of bondage.
                        Faith can become a living center or remain only a language
                        spoken around unchanged priorities.
                    </p>

                    <blockquote class="tributaries-quote">
                        Balance does not mean giving every area equal time.
                        It means refusing to let one area quietly destroy all the others.
                    </blockquote>

                    <p>
                        The purpose of this map is not to become perfect in eleven
                        categories.
                    </p>

                    <p>
                        It is to notice what each stream is carrying into the life
                        they all share.
                    </p>

                </div>

            </div>

        </section>


        <section class="tributaries-principles">

            <div class="section-shell">

                <div class="tributaries-section-heading tributaries-principles-heading">

                    <p class="section-label light-label">
                        Principles of the tributaries
                    </p>

                    <h2>
                        The whole life must be considered.
                    </h2>

                </div>


                <div class="tributaries-principles-grid">


                    <article class="tributaries-principle-card">

                        <span>
                            01
                        </span>

                        <h3>
                            Strength in one area cannot excuse neglect in another.
                        </h3>

                        <p>
                            Professional success does not erase damage at home.
                            Spiritual language does not excuse irresponsibility.
                            Financial knowledge does not replace integrity.
                        </p>

                    </article>


                    <article class="tributaries-principle-card">

                        <span>
                            02
                        </span>

                        <h3>
                            Every stream carries both value and danger.
                        </h3>

                        <p>
                            Work can serve or consume. Money can protect or control.
                            knowledge can create wisdom or pride. Discipline can
                            create freedom or become punishment.
                        </p>

                    </article>


                    <article class="tributaries-principle-card">

                        <span>
                            03
                        </span>

                        <h3>
                            Seasons change which tributary needs attention.
                        </h3>

                        <p>
                            Pregnancy, injury, financial pressure, business growth,
                            grief, opportunity, and family needs each change what
                            responsible stewardship requires.
                        </p>

                    </article>


                    <article class="tributaries-principle-card">

                        <span>
                            04
                        </span>

                        <h3>
                            Some streams exist to strengthen the others.
                        </h3>

                        <p>
                            Better systems protect family time. Better health supports
                            meaningful work. Better communication protects relationships.
                            Better financial understanding expands the ability to serve.
                        </p>

                    </article>


                    <article class="tributaries-principle-card">

                        <span>
                            05
                        </span>

                        <h3>
                            Attention determines what receives water.
                        </h3>

                        <p>
                            The areas repeatedly ignored will eventually reveal
                            the consequences of neglect, even when everything still
                            appears successful from a distance.
                        </p>

                    </article>


                    <article class="tributaries-principle-card">

                        <span>
                            06
                        </span>

                        <h3>
                            Every tributary should eventually flow outward.
                        </h3>

                        <p>
                            Knowledge should teach. Strength should protect. Money
                            should provide. Experience should guide. Faith should
                            change how people are loved and served.
                        </p>

                    </article>


                </div>

            </div>

        </section>


        <section class="tributaries-work">

            <div class="section-shell">

                <div class="tributaries-section-heading">

                    <p class="section-label">
                        What will live inside each stream
                    </p>

                    <h2>
                        The Tributaries are the publishing structure of the platform.
                    </h2>

                    <p>
                        As the site grows, each subject will develop into a searchable
                        collection rather than remaining a single introductory card.
                    </p>

                </div>


                <div class="tributaries-work-grid">


                    <article class="tributaries-work-card">

                        <p class="tributaries-work-type">
                            Reflections
                        </p>

                        <h3>
                            Personal writing
                        </h3>

                        <p>
                            Essays and letters exploring what I am learning,
                            questioning, carrying, changing, and trying to understand.
                        </p>

                    </article>


                    <article class="tributaries-work-card">

                        <p class="tributaries-work-type">
                            Videos
                        </p>

                        <h3>
                            Spoken documentation
                        </h3>

                        <p>
                            Video transcripts, extended reflections, related ideas,
                            and the growing daily record of the journey.
                        </p>

                    </article>


                    <article class="tributaries-work-card">

                        <p class="tributaries-work-type">
                            Guides
                        </p>

                        <h3>
                            Practical resources
                        </h3>

                        <p>
                            Structured lessons, explanations, checklists, frameworks,
                            recipes, scripts, systems, and educational material.
                        </p>

                    </article>


                    <article class="tributaries-work-card">

                        <p class="tributaries-work-type">
                            Projects
                        </p>

                        <h3>
                            Work shown in progress
                        </h3>

                        <p>
                            The website, books, video series, future brokerages,
                            physical transformation, ministry, and systems documented
                            as they are built.
                        </p>

                    </article>


                    <article class="tributaries-work-card">

                        <p class="tributaries-work-type">
                            Collections
                        </p>

                        <h3>
                            Connected bodies of work
                        </h3>

                        <p>
                            Related writings and videos gathered into larger subjects,
                            series, courses, books, and long-term learning paths.
                        </p>

                    </article>


                    <article class="tributaries-work-card">

                        <p class="tributaries-work-type">
                            Recommendations
                        </p>

                        <h3>
                            Tools worth carrying
                        </h3>

                        <p>
                            Books, equipment, services, ingredients, technology,
                            training resources, and partnerships that have proven
                            useful enough to share.
                        </p>

                    </article>


                </div>

            </div>

        </section>


        <section class="tributaries-balance">

            <div class="reading-shell">

                <p class="section-label light-label">
                    The balance of the river
                </p>

                <h2>
                    I am not trying to maximize every area of life at the same time.
                </h2>

                <p class="tributaries-balance-lead">
                    I am trying to keep every area flowing toward the same purpose.
                </p>

                <p>
                    There will be seasons when work requires more.
                </p>

                <p>
                    There will be seasons when family requires nearly everything.
                </p>

                <p>
                    There will be seasons of physical rebuilding, financial
                    concentration, spiritual correction, creative expansion,
                    or quiet preparation.
                </p>

                <p>
                    Balance is not a frozen distribution of time.
                </p>

                <p>
                    It is the ability to adjust without forgetting what the larger
                    life is supposed to protect.
                </p>

                <blockquote class="tributaries-balance-quote">
                    The strongest river is not the one with the most water in a
                    single stream. It is the one whose streams continue feeding
                    the same direction.
                </blockquote>

            </div>

        </section>


